3. Press on the platform by raising your heels as you Expirez by extending your chevilles as high as possible and flexing your calf. Ensure that the genou is kept stationary en permanence. There should be no bending at any time. Hold the contracted position by a second before you start to go back down.
4. Go back Lentement, to the position de départ as you Inspirez by lowering your heels as you bend the chevilles until mollets are stretched.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Calf_Press_On_The_Leg_Press_Machine/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Calf Raise On A Dumbbell', 'Mollets', 'Haltères', '1. Hang on to a sturdy object for balance and stand on a haltère handle, preferably one with round plates so that it rolls as in this manner you have to work harder to stabilize yourself; thus increasing the effectiveness of the exercise.
2. Now roll your foot slightly forward so that you can get a nice stretch of the calf. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Lift the calf as you roll your foot over the top of the handle so that you get a full extension. Expirez during the execution of this movement. Contract the calf hard at the top and Maintenez la position 1 seconde. Conseil : As you come up, roll the haltère slightly backward.
4. Now inspirez as you roll the haltère slightly forward as you come down to get a better stretch.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Calf_Raise_On_A_Dumbbell/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Calf Raises - With Bands', 'Mollets', 'Élastique', '1. Grab an exercise band and stand on it with your toes making sure that the length of the band between the foot and the arms is the same for both sides.
2. While holding the handles of the band, raise the arms to the side of votre tête as if you were getting ready to perform a épaule press. The palms should be facing forward with the coudes bent and to the sides. This movement will create tension on the band. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Keeping the hands by your épaule, Levez-vous on your toes as you expirez and contract the mollets hard at the top of le mouvement.
4. After a one second contraction, Lentement, go back down to the position de départ.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Calf_Raises_-_With_Bands/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Calf Stretch Elbows Against Wall', 'Mollets', 'Autre', '1. Stand facing a wall from a couple feet away.
2. Lean against the wall, placing your poids on your forearms.
3. Attempt to keep your heels on the ground. Maintenez 10-20 secondes. You may move further or closer the wall, making it more or less difficult, respectively.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Calf_Stretch_Elbows_Against_Wall/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Calf Stretch Hands Against Wall', 'Mollets', 'Autre', '1. Stand facing a wall from several feet away. Stagger your stance, placing one foot forward.
2. Lean forward and rest vos mains on the wall, keeping your heel, hanche and head in a straight line.
3. Attempt to keep your heel on the ground. Maintenez 10-20 secondes and then switch sides.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Calf_Stretch_Hands_Against_Wall/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Calves-SMR', 'Mollets', 'Foam roller', '1. Begin seated on le sol. Place a foam roller underneath your lower leg. Your other leg can either be crossed over the opposite or be placed on le sol, supporting some of your poids. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Place vos mains to your side or just behind you, and press down to raise your hanches off of le sol, placing much of your poids against your calf muscle. Roll from below the genou to above the cheville, pausing at points of tension for 10-30 seconds. Répétez de l''autre côté.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Calves-SMR/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Car Deadlift', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. This event apparatus typically has neutral grip handles, however some have a straight bar that you can approach like a normal deadlift. The apparatus can be loaded with a vehicle or other heavy objects such as tractor tires or kegs.
2. Center yourself between the handles if you are a strong squatter, or back a couple inches if you are a strong deadlifter. You feet should be about hanche width apart. Bend at the hanche to grip the handles. With vos pieds and your grip set, take a big breath and then lower your hanches and flex the genous.
3. Look forward with votre tête, keep your poitrine up and votre dos arched, and begin driving through the heels to move the poids upward. As the poids comes up, pull your omoplates together as you drive your hanches forward.
4. Lower the poids by bending at the hanches and guiding it to le sol.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Car_Deadlift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Car Drivers', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. While standing upright, hold a barre plate in both hands at the 3 and 9 o''clock positions. Your palms should be facing each other and vos bras should be extended straight out in front of you. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Initiate le mouvement by rotating the plate as far to one side as possible. Use the same type of movement you would use to turn a steering wheel to one side.
3. Reverse the motion, turning it all the way to the opposite side.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Car_Drivers/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Carioca Quick Step', 'Adducteurs', 'Autre', '1. Begin with vos pieds a few inches apart and your left arm up in a relaxed, athletic position.
2. With your right foot, quick step behind and pull the genou up.
3. Fire vos bras back up when you pull the right genou, being sure that your genou goes straight up and down. Avoid turning vos pieds as you move and continue to look forward as you move to the side.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Abducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Quadriceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Carioca_Quick_Step/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cat Stretch', 'Bas du dos', 'Autre', '1. Position yourself on le sol on vos mains and genous.
2. Pull your belly in and round your spine, lower back, épaules, and neck, letting votre tête drop.
3. Maintenez 15- secondes.', 'Muscles secondaires : Milieu du dos, Trapèzes. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cat_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Catch and Overhead Throw', 'Dos', 'Medecine ball', '1. Begin standing while facing a wall or a partner.
2. Using both hands, position the ball behind votre tête, stretching as much as possible, and forcefully throw the ball forward.
3. Ensure that you follow your throw through, being prepared to receive your rebound from your throw. If you are throwing against the wall, make sure that you stand close enough to the wall to receive the rebound, and aim a little higher than you would with a partner.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Catch_and_Overhead_Throw/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Chain Handle Extension', 'Triceps', 'Autre', '1. You will need two cable handle attachments and a flat banc, as well as chains, for cet exercice. Clip the middle of the chains to the handles, and position yourself on the flat banc. Your coudes should be pointing straight up.
2. Begin by extending through the coude, keeping your upper arm still, with your poignets pronated.
3. Pause at the lockout, and reverse the motion to Revenez en position de départ.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Chain_Handle_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Chain Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Autre', '1. Begin by connecting the chains to the cable handle attachments. Position yourself on the flat banc in the same position as for a haltère press. Your poignets should be pronated and arms perpendiculaire à le sol. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Lower the chains by flexing the coudes, unloading some of the chain onto le sol.
3. Continue until your coude forms a angle de 90 degrés, and then reverse the motion by extending through the coude to lockout.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Chain_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Chair Leg Extended Stretch', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. Sit upright in a chair and grip the seat on the sides.
2. Raise one leg, extending the genou, flexing the cheville as you do so.
3. Lentement, move that leg outward as far as you can, and then back to the center and down.
4. Répétez for your other leg.', 'Muscles secondaires : Adducteurs. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Chair_Leg_Extended_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Chair Lower Back Stretch', 'Dos', 'Autre', '1. Sit upright on a chair.
2. Bend to one side with your arm over votre tête. You can hold onto the chair with your free hand.
3. Maintenez 10- secondes, and Répétez for your other side.', 'Muscles secondaires : Bas du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Chair_Lower_Back_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Chair Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. To begin, first set the bar to a position that best matches your height. Once the bar is loaded, step under it and position it across the back of your épaules.
2. Take the bar with vos mains facing forward, unlock it and lift it off the rack by extending vos jambes.
3. Move vos pieds forward about 18 inches in front of the bar. Position vos jambes using a épaule width stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Look forward en permanence and maintain a neutral or slightly arched spine. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Lentement, lower the bar by bending the genous as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper and lower leg breaks 90 degrees.
5. Begin to raise the bar as you expirez by pushing le sol with the heels of vos pieds, extending the genous and returning to the position de départ.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Chair_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Chair Upper Body Stretch', 'Épaules', 'Autre', '1. Sit on the edge of a chair, gripping the back of it.
2. Straighten vos bras, keeping votre dos straight, and pull your upper body forward so you feel a stretch. Maintenez 20-30 secondes.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Pectoraux. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Chair_Upper_Body_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Chest And Front Of Shoulder Stretch', 'Pectoraux', 'Autre', '1. Start off by standing with vos jambes together, holding a bodybar or a broomstick.
2. Take a slightly wider than épaule width grip on the pole and hold it in front of you with your paumes vers down.
3. Carefully lift the pole up and behind votre tête.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Chest_And_Front_Of_Shoulder_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Chest Push from 3 point stance', 'Pectoraux', 'Medecine ball', '1. Begin in a three point stance, squatted down with votre dos flat and one hand on the ground. Place the medicine ball directly in front of you.
2. To begin, take your first step as you pull the ball to your poitrine, positioning both hands to prepare for the throw.
3. As you execute the second step, explosively release the ball forward as hard as possible.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Chest_Push_from_3_point_stance/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Chest Push (multiple response)', 'Pectoraux', 'Medecine ball', '1. Begin in a kneeling position facing a wall or utilize a partner. Hold the ball with both hands tight into the poitrine.
2. Execute the pass by exploding forward and outward with the hanches while pushing the ball as hard as possible.
3. Follow through by falling forward, catching yourself with vos mains.
4. Immediately return to an upright position. Répétez for the desired number of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Chest_Push_multiple_response/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Chest Push (single response)', 'Pectoraux', 'Medecine ball', '1. Begin in a kneeling position holding the medicine ball with both hands tightly into the poitrine.
2. Execute the pass by exploding forward and outward with the hanches while pushing the ball as far as possible.
3. Follow through by falling forward, catching yourself with vos mains.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Chest_Push_single_response/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Chest Push with Run Release', 'Pectoraux', 'Medecine ball', '1. Begin in an athletic stance with the genous bent, hanches back, and back flat. Hold the medicine ball near vos jambes. C''est votre position de départ.
2. While taking your first step draw the medicine ball into your poitrine.
3. As you take the second step, explosively push the ball forward, immediately sprinting for 10 yards after the release. If you are really fast, you can catch your own pass!', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Chest_Push_with_Run_Release/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Chest Stretch on Stability Ball', 'Pectoraux', 'Swiss ball', '1. Get on vos mains and genous next to an exercise ball.
2. Place your coudes on top of the ball, keeping your arm out to your side. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Lower your torse towards le sol, keeping your coude on top of the ball. Hold the stretch for 20-30 seconds, and Répétez with the other arm.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Chest_Stretch_on_Stability_Ball/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Child''s Pose', 'Bas du dos', 'Autre', '1. Get on vos mains and genous, walk vos mains in front of you.
2. Lower your buttocks down to sit on your heels. Let vos bras drag along le sol as you sit back to stretch your entire spine.
3. Once you settle onto your heels, bring vos mains next to vos pieds and relax. "breathe" into votre dos. Rest your forehead on le sol. Avoid this position if you have genou problems.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Milieu du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Childs_Pose/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Chin-Up', 'Dos', 'Poids de corps', '1. Grab the pull-up bar with the paumes vers your torse and a grip closer than the épaule width.
2. As you have both arms extended in front of you holding the bar at the chosen grip width, keep your torse as straight as possible while creating a curvature on your lower back and sticking your poitrine out. C''est votre position de départ. Conseil : Keeping the torse as straight as possible maximizes biceps stimulation while minimizing back involvement.
3. As you Expirez, pull your torse up until votre tête is around the level of the pull-up bar. Concentrate on using the biceps muscles in order to perform le mouvement. Keep the coudes close to votre corps. Conseil : The upper torse should remain stationary as it moves through space and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work other than hold the bar.
4. After a second of squeezing the biceps in the contracted position, Lentement, lower your torse back to the position de départ; when vos bras are fully extended. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement.
5. Répétez this motion for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Avant-bras, Milieu du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Chin-Up/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Chin To Chest Stretch', 'Cou', 'Autre', '1. Get into a seated position on le sol.
2. Place both hands at the rear of votre tête, fingers interlocked, thumbs pointing down and coudes pointing straight ahead. Lentement, pull votre tête down to your poitrine. Maintenez 20-30 secondes.', 'Muscles secondaires : Trapèzes. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Chin_To_Chest_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Circus Bell', 'Épaules', 'Autre', '1. The circus bell is an oversized haltère with a thick handle. Begin with the haltère between vos pieds, and grip the handle with both hands.
2. Clean the haltère by extending through your hanches and genous to deliver the implement to the desired épaule, letting go with the extra hand.
3. Ensure that you get one of the haltère heads behind the épaule to keep from being thrown off balance. To raise it overhead, dip by flexing the genous, and the drive upwards as you extend the haltère overhead, leaning slightly away from it as you do so.
4. Carefully guide the bell back to le sol, keeping it under control as much as possible. It is best to perform this event on a thick rubber mat to prevent damage to le sol.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Trapèzes, Triceps. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Circus_Bell/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Clean', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. With a barre on le sol close to the shins, take an overhand (or hook) grip just outside the legs. Lower your hanches with the poids focused on the heels, back straight, head facing forward, poitrine up, with your épaules just in front of the bar. C''est votre position de départ.
2. 
3. Begin the first pull by driving through the heels, extending your genous. votre dos angle should stay the same, and vos bras should remain straight. Move the poids with control as you continue to above the genous.
4. Next comes the second pull, the main source of acceleration for the clean. As the bar approaches the mid-cuisse position, begin extending through the hanches. In a jumping motion, accelerate by extending the hanches, genous, and chevilles, using speed to move the bar upward. There should be no need to actively pull through the arms to accelerate the poids; at the end of the second pull, the body should be fully extended, leaning slightly back, with the arms still extended.
5. As full extension is achieved, transition into the third pull by aggressively shrugging and flexing the arms with the coudes up and out. At peak extension, aggressively pull yourself down, rotating your coudes under the bar as you do so. Receive the bar in a front squat position, the depth of which is dependent upon the height of the bar at the end of the third pull. The bar should be racked onto the protracted épaules, lightly touching the throat with the hands relaxed. Continue to descend to the bottom squat position, which will help in the recovery.
6. Immediately recover by driving through the heels, keeping the torse upright and coudes up. Continue until you have risen to a standing position.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Épaules, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Clean/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Clean Deadlift', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. Begin standing with a barre close to your shins. vos pieds should be directly under your hanches with vos pieds turned out slightly. Grip the bar with a double prise en pronation or hook grip, about épaule width apart. Squat down to the bar. Your spine should be in full extension, with a back angle that places your épaules in front of the bar and votre dos as vertical as possible.
2. Begin by driving through le sol through the front of your heels. As the bar travels upward, maintain a constant back angle. Flare your genous out to the side to help keep them out of the bar''s path.
3. After the bar crosses the genous, complete the lift by driving the hanches into the bar until your hanches and genous are extended.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Milieu du dos, Quadriceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Clean_Deadlift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Clean Pull', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. With a barre on le sol close to the shins, take an overhand or hook grip just outside the legs. Lower your hanches with the poids focused on the heels, back straight, head facing forward, poitrine up, with your épaules just in front of the bar. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin the first pull by driving through the heels, extending your genous. votre dos angle should stay the same, and vos bras should remain straight and coudes out. Move the poids with control as you continue to above the genous.
3. Next comes the second pull, the main source of acceleration for the clean. As the bar approaches the mid-cuisse position, begin extending through the hanches. In a jumping motion, accelerate by extending the hanches, genous, and chevilles, using speed to move the bar upward. There should be no need to actively pull through the arms to accelerate the poids; at the end of the second pull, the body should be fully extended, leaning slightly back, with the arms still extended. Full extension should be violent and abrupt, and ensure that you do not prolong the extension for longer than necessary.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Clean_Pull/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Clean Shrug', 'Trapèzes', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a épaule width, double overhand or hook grip, with the bar hanging at the mid cuisse position. votre dos should be straight and inclined slightly forward.
2. Shrug your épaules towards your ears. While cet exercice can usually by loaded with heavier poids than a clean, avoid overloading to the point that the execution slows down.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Clean_Shrug/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Clean and Jerk', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. With a barre on le sol close to the shins, take an overhand or hook grip just outside the legs. Lower your hanches with the poids focused on the heels, back straight, head facing forward, poitrine up, with your épaules just in front of the bar. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin the first pull by driving through the heels, extending your genous. votre dos angle should stay the same, and vos bras should remain straight. Move the poids with control as you continue to above the genous.
3. Next comes the second pull, the main source of acceleration for the clean. As the bar approaches the mid-cuisse position, begin extending through the hanches. In a jumping motion, accelerate by extending the hanches, genous, and chevilles, using speed to move the bar upward. There should be no need to actively pull through the arms to accelerate the poids; at the end of the second pull, the body should be fully extended, leaning slightly back, with the arms still extended.
4. As full extension is achieved, transition into the third pull by aggressively shrugging and flexing the arms with the coudes up and out. At peak extension, aggressively pull yourself down, rotating your coudes under the bar as you do so. Receive the bar in a front squat position, the depth of which is dependent upon the height of the bar at the end of the third pull. The bar should be racked onto the protracted épaules, lightly touching the throat with the hands relaxed. Continue to descend to the bottom squat position, which will help in the recovery.
5. Immediately recover by driving through the heels, keeping the torse upright and coudes up. Continue until you have risen to a standing position.
6. The second phase is the jerk, which raises the poids overhead. Standing with the poids racked on the front of the épaules, begin with the dip. With vos pieds directly under your hanches, flex the genous without moving the hanches backward. Go down only slightly, and reverse direction as powerfully as possible.
7. Drive through the heels create as much speed and force as possible, and be sure to move votre tête out of the way as the bar leaves the épaules.
8. At this moment as the feet leave le sol, the feet must be placed into the receiving position as quickly as possible. In the brief moment the feet are not actively driving against the platform, the athletes effort to push the bar up will drive them down. The feet should be split, with one foot forward, and one foot back. Receive the bar with the arms locked out overhead. Return to a standing position.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Trapèzes, Triceps. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Clean_and_Jerk/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Clean and Press', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. Assume a épaule-width stance, with genous inside the arms. Now while keeping the back flat, bend at the genous and hanches so that you can grab the bar with the arms fully extended and a pronated grip that is slightly wider than épaule width. Point the coudes out to sides. The bar should be close to the shins. Position the épaules over or slightly ahead of the bar. Establish a flat back posture. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin to pull the bar by extending the genous. Move your hanches forward and raise the épaules at the same rate while keeping the angle of the back constant; continue to lift the bar straight up while keeping it close to votre corps.
3. As the bar passes the genou, extend at the chevilles, genous, and hanches forcefully, similar to a jumping motion. As you do so, continue to guide the bar with vos mains, shrugging your épaules and using the momentum from your movement to pull the bar as high as possible. The bar should travel close to votre corps, and you should keep your coudes out.
4. At maximum elevation, vos pieds should clear le sol and you should start to pull yourself under the bar. The mechanics of this could change slightly, depending on the poids used. You should descend into a squatting position as you pull yourself under the bar.
5. As the bar hits terminal height, rotate your coudes around and under the bar. Rack the bar across the front of the épaules while keeping the torse erect and flexing the hanches and genous to absorb the poids of the bar.
6. Stand to full height, holding the bar in the clean position.
7. Without moving vos pieds, press the bar overhead as you expirez. Lower the bar under control .', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Milieu du dos, Quadriceps, Épaules, Trapèzes, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Clean_and_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Clean from Blocks', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. With a barre on boxes or stands of the desired height, take an overhand or hook grip just outside the legs. Lower your hanches with the poids focused on the heels, back straight, head facing forward, poitrine up, with your épaules just in front of the bar. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin the first pull by driving through the heels, extending your genous. votre dos angle should stay the same, and vos bras should remain straight with the coudes pointed out.
3. As full extension is achieved, transition into the receiving position by aggressively shrugging and flexing the arms with the coudes up and out. Aggressively pull yourself down, rotating your coudes under the bar as you do so. Receive the bar in a front squat position, the depth of which is dependent upon the height of the bar at the end of the third pull. The bar should be racked onto the protracted épaules, lightly touching the throat with the hands relaxed. Continue to descend to the bottom squat position, which will help in the recovery.
4. Immediately recover by driving through the heels, keeping the torse upright and coudes up. Continue until you have risen to a standing position. Return the poids to the boxes for the next rep.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Épaules, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Clean_from_Blocks/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Clock Push-Up', 'Pectoraux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Move into a prone position on le sol, supporting your poids on vos mains and toes.
2. vos bras should be fully extended with the hands around épaule width. Keep votre corps straight throughout le mouvement. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Descend by flexing at the coude, lowering your poitrine toward the ground.
4. At the bottom, reverse the motion by pushing yourself up through coude extension as quickly as possible until you are air borne. Aim to "jump" 12-18 inches to one side.
5. As you accelerate up, move your outside foot away from your direction of travel. Leaving the ground, shift votre corps about 30 degrees for the next repetition.
6. Revenez en position de départ and Répétez the exercise, working all the way around until you are back where you started.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Clock_Push-Up/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Close-Grip Barbell Bench Press', 'Triceps', 'Barre', '1. Allongez-vous au sol on a flat banc. Using a close grip (around épaule width), lift the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with vos bras locked. C''est votre position de départ.
2. As you Inspirez, come down Lentement, until you feel the bar on your middle poitrine. Conseil : Make sure that - as opposed to a regular banc press - you keep the coudes close to the torse en permanence in order to maximize triceps involvement.
3. Après une pause, bring the bar back to the position de départ as you Expirez and push the bar using your triceps muscles. Lock vos bras in the contracted position, Maintenez la position 1 seconde and then start coming down Lentement, again. Conseil : It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up.
4. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.
5. When you are done, place the bar back in the rack.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Close-Grip_Barbell_Bench_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Close-Grip Dumbbell Press', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. Place a haltère standing up on a flat banc.
2. Ensuring that the haltère stays securely placed at the top of the banc, lie perpendiculaire à the banc with only your épaules lying on the surface. hanches should be below the banc and vos jambes bent with vos pieds firmly on le sol.
3. Grasp the haltère with both hands and hold it straight over your poitrine at arm''s length. Both palms should be pressing against the underside of the sides of the haltère. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Initiate le mouvement by lowering the haltère to your poitrine.
5. Revenez en position de départ by extending the coudes.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Close-Grip_Dumbbell_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Close-Grip EZ-Bar Curl with Band', 'Biceps', 'Barre EZ', '1. Attach a band to each end of the bar. Take the bar, placing a foot on the middle of the band. Levez-vousright with a narrow, supinated grip on the EZ bar. The coudes should be close to the torse. C''est votre position de départ.
2. While keeping the upper arms in place, flex the coudes to execute the curl. Expirez as the poids is lifted.
3. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entièrement contracté and the bar is at épaule level. Maintenez la position 1 seconde and squeeze the biceps hard.
4. Lentement, begin to bring the bar back to position de départ as your Inspirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Close-Grip_EZ-Bar_Curl_with_Band/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Close-Grip EZ-Bar Press', 'Triceps', 'Barre EZ', '1. Allongez-vous sur un banc plat with an EZ bar loaded to an appropriate poids.
2. Using a prise serrée lift the bar and hold it straight over your torse with your coudes in. The arms should be perpendiculaire à le sol. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Now lower the bar down to your lower poitrine as you Inspirez. Keep the coudes in as you perform this movement.
4. Using the triceps to push the bar back up, press it back to the position de départ by extending the coudes as you expirez.
5. Répétez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Close-Grip_EZ-Bar_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Close-Grip EZ Bar Curl', 'Biceps', 'Barre', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse upright while holding an E-Z Curl Bar at the closer inner handle. The palm of vos mains should be facing forward and they should be slightly tilted inwards due to the shape of the bar. The coudes should be close to the torse. C''est votre position de départ.
2. While holding the upper arms stationary, curl the poids forward while contracting the biceps as you Expirez. Conseil : Only the forearms should move.
3. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entièrement contracté and the bar is at épaule level. Maintenez la position 1 seconde and squeeze the biceps hard.
4. Lentement, begin to bring the bar back to position de départ as your Inspirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Close-Grip_EZ_Bar_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Close-Grip Front Lat Pulldown', 'Dos', 'Poulie', '1. Sit down on a pull-down machine with a wide bar attached to the top pulley. Make sure that you adjust the genou pad of the machine to fit your height. These pads will prevent votre corps from being raised by the resistance attached to the bar.
2. Grab the bar with the paumes vers l''avant using the prescribed grip. Note on grips: For a prise large, vos mains need to be spaced out at a distance wider than your épaule width. For a prise moyenne, vos mains need to be spaced out at a distance equal to your épaule width and for a close grip at a distance smaller than your épaule width.
3. As you have both arms extended in front of you - while holding the bar at the chosen grip width - bring your torse back around 30 degrees or so while creating a curvature on your lower back and sticking your poitrine out. C''est votre position de départ.
4. As you Expirez, bring the bar down until it touches your upper poitrine by drawing the épaules and the upper arms down and back. Conseil : Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the full contracted position. The upper torse should remain stationary (only the arms should move). The forearms should do no other work except for holding the bar; therefore do not try to pull the bar down using the forearms.
5. After a second in the contracted position, while squeezing your omoplates together, Lentement, raise the bar back to the position de départ when vos bras are fully extended and the lats are fully stretched. Inspirez during this portion of le mouvement.
6. 6. Répétez this motion for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Close-Grip_Front_Lat_Pulldown/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Close-Grip Push-Up off of a Dumbbell', 'Triceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Allongez-vous au sol and place vos mains on an upright haltère. Supporting your poids on your toes and hands, keep your torse rigid and your coudes in with vos bras straight. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Lower votre corps, allowing the coudes to flex while you inspirez. Keep votre corps straight, not allowing your hanches to rise or sag.
3. Press yourself back up to the position de départ by extending the coudes. Expirez as you perform this step.
4. Après une pause, at the contracted position, Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Close-Grip_Push-Up_off_of_a_Dumbbell/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Close-Grip Standing Barbell Curl', 'Biceps', 'Barre', '1. Hold a barre with both hands, palms up and a few inches apart.
2. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse straight and votre tête up. vos pieds should be about épaule width and your coudes close to your torse. C''est votre position de départ. Conseil : You will keep your upper arms and coudes stationary throughout le mouvement.
3. Curl the bar up in a semicircular motion until the forearms touch your biceps. Expirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement and contract your biceps hard for a second at the top. Conseil : Avoid bending the back or using swinging motions as you lift the poids. Only the forearms should move.
4. Lentement, go back down to the position de départ as you inspirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Close-Grip_Standing_Barbell_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cocoons', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Begin by lying on votre dos on the ground. vos jambes should be straight and vos bras extended behind votre tête. C''est votre position de départ.
2. To perform le mouvement, tuck the genous toward your poitrine, rotating your pelvis to lift your fessiers from le sol. As you do so, flex the spine, bringing vos bras back over votre tête to perform a simultaneous crunch motion.
3. Après une pause, Revenez en position de départ.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cocoons/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Conan''s Wheel', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. With the poids loaded, take a zurcher hold on the end of the implement. Place the bar in the crook of the coude and hold onto your poignet. Try to keep the poids off of the forearms.
2. Begin by lifting the poids from the ground. Keep a tight, upright posture as you being to walk, taking short, fast steps. Look up and away as you turn in a circle. Do not hold your breath during the event. Continue walking until you complete one or more complete turns.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Biceps, Mollets, Avant-bras, Bas du dos, Épaules, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Conans_Wheel/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Concentration Curls', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Sit down on a flat banc with one haltère in front of you between vos jambes. vos jambes should be spread with your genous bent and feet on le sol.
2. Use your right arm to pick the haltère up. Place the back of your right upper arm on the top of your inner right cuisse. Rotate the palm of your hand until it is facing forward away from your cuisse. Conseil : Your arm should be extended and the haltère should be above le sol. C''est votre position de départ.
3. While holding the upper arm stationary, curl the poids forward while contracting the biceps as you Expirez. Only the forearms should move. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entièrement contracté and the haltères are at épaule level. Conseil : At the top of le mouvement make sure that the little finger of your arm is higher than your thumb. This guarantees a good contraction. Maintenez la position 1 seconde as you squeeze the biceps.
4. Lentement, begin to bring the haltères back to position de départ as your Inspirez. Caution: Avoid swinging motions at any time.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité. Then Répétez le mouvement with the left arm.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Concentration_Curls/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cross-Body Crunch', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Allongez-vous au sol and bend your genous about 60 degrees.
2. Keep vos pieds flat on le sol and place vos mains loosely behind votre tête. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Now curl up and bring your right coude and épaule across votre corps while bring your left genou in toward your left épaule at the same time. Reach with your coude and try to touch your genou. Expirez as you perform this movement. Conseil : Try to bring your épaule up towards your genou rather than just your coude and remember that the key is to contract the abdominaux as you perform le mouvement; not just to move the coude.
4. Now go back down to the position de départ as you inspirez and Répétez with the left coude and the right genou.
5. Continue alternating in this manner until all prescribed repetitions are done.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cross-Body_Crunch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cross Body Hammer Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec a haltère in each hand. vos mains should be down at your side with your paumes vers in.
2. While keeping your paumes vers in and without twisting your arm, curl the haltère of the right arm up towards your left épaule as you expirez. Touch the top of the haltère to your épaule and hold the contraction for a second.
3. Lentement, lower the haltère along the same path as you inspirez and then Répétez the same movement for the left arm.
4. Continue alternating in this fashion until the recommended amount of repetitions is performed for each arm.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cross_Body_Hammer_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cross Over - With Bands', 'Pectoraux', 'Élastique', '1. Secure an exercise band around a stationary post.
2. While facing away from the post, grab the handles on both ends of the band and step forward enough to create tension on the band.
3. Raise vos bras to the sides, parallèle au sol, perpendiculaire à your torse (your torse and the arms should resemble the letter "T") and with the paumes vers l''avant. Have them extended with a slight bend at the coudes. C''est votre position de départ.
4. While keeping vos bras straight, bring them across your poitrine in a semicircular motion to the front as you expirez and flex your pecs. Hold the contraction for a second.
5. Lentement, Revenez en position de départ as you inspirez.
6. Perform for the recommended amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cross_Over_-_With_Bands/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Crossover Reverse Lunge', 'Bas du dos', 'Autre', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec vos pieds épaule width apart. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Perform a rear lunge by stepping back with one foot and flexing the hanches and front genou. As you do so, rotate your torse across the front leg.
3. Après une pause, Revenez en position de départ and Répétez de l''autre côté, continuing in an alternating fashion.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Abducteurs, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Quadriceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Crossover_Reverse_Lunge/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Crucifix', 'Épaules', 'Autre', '1. In the crucifix, you statically hold poids out to the side for time. While the event can be practiced using haltères, it is best to practice with one of the various implements used, such as axes and hammers, as it feels different.
